          deepDive: "**〜ぶる** makes a verb meaning *to put on airs of ~, to act as if one were ~* when in fact one isn't: 上品ぶる (*act all refined*), 大人ぶる (*act grown-up*), いい子ぶる (*play the goody-goody*). The book: 実際はそうではないのに、そのように見せている. The speaker sees the behavior as fake or unjustified, so the tone is critical or mocking.\n\nConnection: **N / なA / いA (drop い) + ぶる**: 優等生ぶる, 悪者ぶる, 上品ぶる, 偉い → 偉ぶる, 悪い → 悪ぶる. The ＊ note lists the usual words: 優等生・悪者・大人・上品・いい子・偉い. Others you'll meet: 先輩ぶる, 通ぶる (*act like a connoisseur*), 学者ぶる, お嬢様ぶる.\n\nGrammar: ぶる conjugates as a Group I verb (＊): ぶらない, ぶって, ぶった, ぶっている.\n- **〜ぶって**: 大人ぶって難しい言葉を使っている (*using difficult words, acting all grown-up*).\n- **〜ぶってもしょうがない** (sample): *there's no point acting ~*: 食べ放題で上品ぶってもしょうがないだろ？\n- **いくら〜ぶっても**: いくら若い子ぶっても年はごまかせなかった (*however much I acted like a young girl, I couldn't hide my age*).\n- **〜ぶったところがない**: 少しも偉ぶったところがない (*doesn't put on airs at all*). Negated, it becomes praise: *down-to-earth*.\n\nNuance: ぶる is about **image and status**, seeming more mature, grand, refined, innocent or tough than one is. It's casual and judgmental (the book's grumbling face). Said about yourself, it's self-mocking: 昔ぼくは好きな女の子の前で悪ぶっていた (*I used to act like a bad boy in front of girls I liked*).\n\nLook-alikes (not taught as numbered points):\n- **〜ふりをする**: neutral pretending, for any action or state: 寝たふりをする (*pretend to be asleep*), 知らないふりをする. ぶる doesn't attach to verbs: ✗寝ぶる.\n- **〜っぽい**: 子どもっぽい (*childish*) describes a quality someone actually shows; 大人ぶる is a pose someone puts on.\n- **〜がる**: 寒がる, 欲しがる show someone's real feelings, not a fake status.\n- **〜ぶり**: 久しぶり (*after a long time*), 仕事ぶり (*the way someone works*) is a different suffix.\n\nCommon mistakes:\n- Attaching it to a verb: ✗知るぶる → ✓物知りぶる / 知ったかぶりをする.\n- Keeping the い: ✗偉いぶる → ✓偉ぶる.\n\nJLPT tip: in 問題2, ぶる attaches to the word right before it, so pair the noun or adjective with ぶって / ぶっても first (若い子 + ぶっても). In a Check-style blank, a noun like 大人 followed by a description of show-off behavior calls for ぶって.",
